{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocityVariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocityVariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.variance_ordering_records","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.variance_ordering_records","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocityVariance.lean#L54-L67","doc":"The variance scoreboard on PR #801, all at `w_λ = dim_q²/[n]_q!`:\neach baseline's max/min ratio is recorded.\n\n- tensor-product baseline (rejected): 3.96× — wrong sign on T/³He\n- mass-endomorphism blow-up (D/T/³He): 2.31×\n- depth-stratified α_k·Φ_k (D/T/³He/⁴He): 1.82× — best\n- block-multiplicative scaling (16 atoms): 5.47-10.99×\n\nThe depth-stratified result is the tightest categorical\nstructure on the chain; the FR refinement (this conjecture) is\nthe proposed mechanism to close further. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.fr_simpler_forms_variance_records","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.fr_simpler_forms_variance_records","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocityVariance.lean#L37-L50","doc":"Empirical record of falsifications, all at `w_λ = dim_q²/[n]_q!`.\n\nThe |χ^λ|^β weighting (β ∈ [-2, 2]) was tested and gave\nvariance worsening from 1.82× (uniform baseline) to 2.30-3.00×\nat β > 0, falsifying the simple magnitude-weight hypothesis.\n\nThe self-conjugate restriction gave variance 5.94×,\nfalsifying the Wenzl-bridge-stratum hypothesis.\n\nThese observed variance values exceed the uniform baseline\n1.82×, recorded here as a verified comparison. ","signatureChunk":0}]}